/given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Barash</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Expression of albumin in nonhepatic tissues and its synthesis by the bovine mammary gland.</article-title><source>J Dairy Sci</source><volume>88</volume><fpage>569</fpage><lpage>576</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15653522</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002829-deVijlder1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Vijlder</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Veenboer</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dijk</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Thyroid albumin originates from blood.</article-title><source>Endocrinology</source><volume>131</volume><fpage>578</fpage><lpage>584</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1639008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002829-Dziarski1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dziarski</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Cell-bound albumin is the 70-kDa peptidoglycan-, lipopolysaccharide-, and lipoteichoic acid-binding protein on lymphocytes and macrophages.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>269</volume><fpage>20431</fpage><lpage>20436</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8051139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002829-Yamaguchi1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamaguchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Igarashi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Misawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsurusaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>2